Rain 很喜欢在戏里吃东西。

305
00:14:41.490 --> 00:14:42.170
He loved it.
他很喜欢。

306
00:14:42.330 --> 00:14:49.110
So whenever he had a chance to just completely chow down on something, I'm sure he was so tickled that he got to do that.
所以每当有机会能大快朵颐时，我敢肯定他一定乐坏了，因为他终于能这么做了。

307
00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:56.870
As actors, have you guys ever heard the sort of criticism of actors that like to munch an apple during the scene?
作为演员，你们有没有听说过那种针对演员的批评，说他们喜欢在戏里嚼苹果？

308
00:14:57.210 --> 00:14:57.610
No.
没有。

309
00:14:57.710 --> 00:14:59.390
What is the criticism of eating an apple?
吃苹果有什么好批评的？

310
00:14:59.530 --> 00:14:59.710
Oh.
哦。

311
00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:02.990
Well, I don't know if it's just a sound department apple?
嗯，我不知道这是否只是录音部门对苹果有意见？

312
00:15:03.290 --> 00:15:07.830
No, it's just like it's a little bit of a crutch for an actor to be able to-
不，这只是演员的一种小手段，为了能够……

313
00:15:07.830 --> 00:15:08.590
Brad Pitt does it all the time.
布拉德·皮特总是这么做。

314
00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:09.190
Does he really?
真的吗？

315
00:15:09.410 --> 00:15:09.670
Yes.
是的。

316
00:15:09.670 --> 00:15:11.050
He eats apples in movies?
他在电影里吃苹果？

317
00:15:11.250 --> 00:15:11.510
No, no, no.
不，不，不。

318
00:15:11.570 --> 00:15:11.870
Food.
是吃东西。

319
00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:13.570
Watch the Ocean's 12 movies.
看看《十一罗汉》系列电影。

320
00:15:13.590 --> 00:15:14.950
He's always eating something.
他总是在吃东西。

321
00:15:15.230 --> 00:15:15.490
Yeah.
没错。

322
00:15:15.490 --> 00:15:20.670
Kind of, it's like a way to appear very casual as you're giving your lines, you're munching away on stuff.
怎么说呢，这就像是一种在念台词时显得很随意的表演方式，一边嚼着东西一边说。

323
00:15:21.330 --> 00:15:21.490
Oh.
哦。

324
00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:22.310
Huh.
嗯。

325
00:15:22.470 --> 00:15:23.690
Angela just threw Brad Pitt under the bus.
安吉拉刚才把布拉德·皮特给卖了。

326
00:15:23.690 --> 00:15:24.890
I didn't mean to throw a chase.
我不是故意要找茬。

327
00:15:25.350 --> 00:15:28.930
He's in front of actors eating and I just was thinking-
他是在演员面前吃东西，我只是在想……

328
00:15:28.930 --> 00:15:29.470
I don't know if it's bad.
我不知道这算不算坏事。

329
00:15:29.470 --> 00:15:30.570
It's just a thing.
这只是一种习惯。

330
00:15:30.710 --> 00:15:36.730
One of my favorite parts of like all of the Godfather movies and Goodfellas movies is how much people eat.
我最喜欢《教父》系列和《好家伙》电影的一点就是里面的人吃得特别多。

331
00:15:36.930 --> 00:15:38.570
The Sopranos eat all the time.
《黑道家族》里的人也一直在吃。

332
00:15:39.070 --> 00:15:39.750
They're always eating.
他们总是在吃东西。

333
00:15:40.030 --> 00:15:40.350
Yeah.
没错。

334
00:15:40.470 --> 00:15:41.390
On the Sopranos.
在《黑道家族》里。

335
00:15:41.910 --> 00:15:43.150
Sure, they have very good catering.
当然，他们的剧组餐饮非常好。

336
00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:48.370
Well, now we're in Michael's office and D'Angelo really wants one of Michael's toys.
好了，现在我们在迈克尔的办公室，迪安杰洛真的很想要迈克尔的一个玩具。

337
00:15:48.650 --> 00:15:53.070
He wants the little 18-wheeler Dunder Mifflin-like paper delivery truck.
他想要那个像邓德·米夫林公司那样的 18 轮纸品运输小卡车。

338
00:15:53.490 --> 00:15:57.950
Michael is clearly annoyed and he says, sure, take my favorite truck.
迈克尔显然很恼火，他说，行啊，拿走我最喜欢的卡车吧。

339
00:15:58.370 --> 00:15:59.690
D'Angelo says, you know what?
迪安杰洛说，你知道吗？

340
00:15:59.730 --> 00:16:00.590
I'm going to give you space.
我要给你留点空间。

341
00:16:00.590 --> 00:16:02.170
I'm going to post up in the break room.
我要去休息室待着。

342
00:16:02.310 --> 00:16:06.310
And then he has a talking head where he says, ugh, dead man walking.
然后他有一个采访镜头，他说，呃，死人走路。

343
00:16:07.110 --> 00:16:12.550
And Greg, I had to know if there was a candy bag alt for this talking head.
格雷格，我得知道这个采访镜头有没有“糖果袋”的备选方案。

344
00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:17.470
And Greg just told me something outside, Jenna, that you didn't hear.
格雷格刚才在外面告诉了我一件事，珍娜，你没听到。

345
00:16:17.650 --> 00:16:19.170
And I can't wait for him to tell you.
我迫不及待想让他告诉你。

346
00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:21.770
Will you tell us that you came up with?
你能告诉我们你是怎么想出来的吗？

347
00:16:22.010 --> 00:16:24.630
Oh, well, candy bag is my term.
哦，那个，“糖果袋”是我自创的词。

348
00:16:25.090 --> 00:16:25.930
He made it up?
是他编出来的？

349
00:16:25.970 --> 00:16:27.170
You made up candy bag?
“糖果袋”是你编的？

350
00:16:27.270 --> 00:16:28.910
Yes, yes, he did.
是的，没错，是他编的。

351
00:16:29.150 --> 00:16:35.710
I was trying to make it sound fun and exciting to the crew that they have to shoot extra material.
我当时在努力让剧组觉得要补拍素材这件事听起来既有趣又令人兴奋。

352
00:16:35.710 --> 00:16:38.030
We couldn't decide what the lines should be.
我们没法决定台词该怎么写。

353
00:16:39.210 --> 00:16:40.010
So, yeah.
所以，就是这样。

354
00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:42.710
Well, it's one of my absolute favorite things.
嗯，这是我最喜欢的事情之一。

355
00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:44.150
And I didn't know you made up that term.
而且我不知道那个词是你编出来的。

356
00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:45.290
And it makes me so happy.
这让我感到非常开心。

357
00:16:45.490 --> 00:16:48.710
And there were candy bag alts for this D'Angelo talking head.
关于迪安杰洛的这段采访，还有好几个糖果袋的备选方案。

358
00:16:48.990 --> 00:16:50.950
I'm going to read you three of my favorites.
我要给你们读三个我最喜欢的。

359
00:16:52.550 --> 00:16:52.950
Blech.
呸。

360
00:16:53.250 --> 00:16:55.090
Be professional for God's sake.
看在上帝的份上，专业点。

361
00:16:55.330 --> 00:16:56.150
Share your toys.
学会分享你的玩具。

362
00:16:57.270 --> 00:16:57.850
That's good.
那很好。

363
00:16:58.070 --> 00:16:58.590
I like that.
我喜欢那个。

364
00:16:58.870 --> 00:16:59.390
Next one.
下一个。

365
00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:02.670
I've been here three weeks and he hasn't touched the truck.
我来这儿三周了，他连碰都没碰过那辆卡车。

366
00:17:05.600 --> 00:17:08.180
And lastly, I don't even want the truck.
最后，我其实根本不想要那辆卡车。

367
00:17:08.320 --> 00:17:09.920
I just want it because he has it.
我只是因为他有，所以才想要。

368
00:17:10.080 --> 00:17:11.140
I'm a helicopter guy.
我是个直升机迷。

369
00:17:11.300 --> 00:17:12.160
I like helicopters.
我喜欢直升机。

370
00:17:12.520 --> 00:17:14.720
I kind of like them all better than what we use.
我觉得它们比我们用的那些都要好。

371
00:17:17.340 --> 00:17:19.240
My favorite is I've been here three weeks.
我最喜欢的是“我来这儿三周了”。

372
00:17:19.340 --> 00:17:20.620
He hasn't even touched the truck.
他连卡车都没碰过。

373
00:17:20.840 --> 00:17:20.980
Yeah.
是啊。

374
00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:23.240
Well, you know what's interesting is this.
嗯，你知道有趣的是这个。

375
00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:28.180
I was looking over this and this was, you know, one of the reasons I really wanted to come in.
我当时在看这个，你知道，这也是我真的很想加入的原因之一。

376
00:17:28.280 --> 00:17:29.720
I was very proud of this script.
我当时对这个剧本非常自豪。

377
00:17:30.120 --> 00:17:31.840
And, you know, it was an Emmy-nominated script.
而且，你知道，这是一个获得艾美奖提名的剧本。

378
00:17:31.840 --> 00:17:37.240
And I feel like I was sort of, you know, running on all cylinders at this point.
我觉得当时我算是，你知道，火力全开。

379
00:17:37.380 --> 00:17:45.720
And there's a lot of times in the script where there's little bits of information that are sort of snuck in that are setting up all these different storylines.
剧本里有很多地方悄悄塞进了一些小信息，为后续的所有剧情线做铺垫。

380
00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:53.240
And I'm sure the reason why we picked Dead Man Walking was because it led into Michael's next talking head where he says, I'm not sad.
我敢肯定我们选择《死囚漫步》的原因，是因为它引出了迈克尔接下来的采访，他说：“我不难过。”

381
00:17:53.240 --> 00:17:55.340
I don't have to leave till tomorrow and tomorrow I'll be a wreck.
“我明天才走，明天我才会崩溃。”

382
00:17:55.340 --> 00:18:04.460
And that is setting up this whole notion of when is he actually leaving, which is Steve's idea.
这其实是在为他到底什么时候走这个概念做铺垫，这是史蒂夫的主意。

383
00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:14.780
And it's like this wonderful way to disguise a lot of the emotional stuff so that people aren't having to talk to him directly as if it's his last day.
这是一种绝妙的方式，掩盖了很多情感上的东西，这样大家就不必直接跟他谈论这是否是他的最后一天。

384
00:18:14.940 --> 00:18:16.980
They're just trying to, you know, have it be a normal day.
他们只是试图，你知道，让这一天过得正常点。

385
00:18:16.980 --> 00:18:17.680
Get through a normal day.
平平淡淡地过完这一天。

386
00:18:17.720 --> 00:18:18.020
Yeah.
是啊。

387
00:18:18.020 --> 00:18:19.820
But he knows it's his last day.
但他知道这就是他的最后一天。

388
00:18:20.520 --> 00:18:25.500
So that's probably why we picked Dead Man Walking instead of those other ones, which sound pretty hilarious.
所以这可能就是我们选择《死囚漫步》而不是其他那些听起来很搞笑的片名的原因。

389
00:18:26.840 --> 00:18:27.900
You're so right, though.
不过你说得太对了。

390
00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:34.540
And I mean, Jenna and I were talking about this as we prepped this episode about how thoughtful you were, Greg, in writing this.
我是说，珍娜和我在准备这一集的时候聊过，格雷格，你写这一集的时候有多用心。

391
00:18:34.740 --> 00:18:40.260
Because there are so many wonderful moments that point back to earlier episodes.
因为里面有太多精彩的瞬间，都呼应了之前的剧集。

392
00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:46.460
And if you watch it with that in mind, I just got so much more emotional watching it.
如果你带着这种想法去看，我在看的时候真的感触良多。

393
00:18:47.460 --> 00:18:47.620
Yeah.
是啊。

394
00:18:47.820 --> 00:18:51.700
I mean, I was so delighted to see that party planning committee scene.
我是说，看到那个派对策划委员会的场景，我真的太高兴了。

395
00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:52.100
Yeah.
是啊。

396
00:18:52.300 --> 00:18:58.600
And to see how differently Michael regarded the party planning committee in this episode compared to the first one.
看到迈克尔在这一集中对待派对策划委员会的态度，与第一集相比有多大的不同，真是太有意思了。

397
00:18:58.720 --> 00:19:05.000
So much so that I pulled audio clips of both the first party planning and this one.
以至于我把第一次派对策划和这次的音频片段都找了出来。

398
00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:06.560
And I thought we could listen to them back to back.
我想我们可以把它们连在一起听听。

399
00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:07.400
Yeah, let's do it.
好，来吧。

400
00:19:07.400 --> 00:19:07.600
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊，是啊。

401
00:19:07.660 --> 00:19:07.920
That's great.
太棒了。

402
00:19:11.240 --> 00:19:13.920
Green, yellow, red.
绿色、黄色、红色。

403
00:19:14.340 --> 00:19:15.020
How about green?
绿色怎么样？

404
00:19:15.480 --> 00:19:17.420
I think green is kind of whorish.
我觉得绿色有点像妓女用的颜色。

405
00:19:18.020 --> 00:19:20.960
These are my party planning biatches.
这些是我的派对策划小婊砸们。

406
00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:23.520
Pulled off an amazing 80s party last year.
去年搞了一场超赞的80年代派对。

407
00:19:23.780 --> 00:19:24.220
Off the hook.
简直绝了。

408
00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:31.380
So I was thinking, if you haven't already gotten a cake, maybe go in for one of those ice cream cakes from Baskin Robbins.
所以我一直在想，如果你还没买蛋糕，也许可以去买那种芭斯罗缤的冰淇淋蛋糕。

409
00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:33.100
They're very good, very delicious.
它们非常好吃，非常美味。

410
00:19:33.460 --> 00:19:35.500
Meredith's allergic to dairy, so...
梅雷迪思对乳制品过敏，所以……

411
00:19:36.060 --> 00:19:38.000
She's not the only one that's going to be eating it, right?
又不是只有她一个人吃，对吧？

412
00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:40.160
And I think everybody likes ice cream cake.
而且我觉得大家都喜欢冰淇淋蛋糕。

413
00:19:41.840 --> 00:19:43.980
That's just about her, so...
那只是针对她个人的，所以……

414
00:19:43.980 --> 00:19:44.540
It is.
确实。

415
00:19:44.800 --> 00:19:47.240
Her chocolate chip would be good.
她的巧克力碎口味应该不错。

416
00:19:47.520 --> 00:19:49.020
How about some...
要不要来点……

417
00:19:50.180 --> 00:19:51.780
So that's the first one.
所以这是第一个。

418
00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:52.220
Yeah.
是啊。

419
00:19:52.520 --> 00:19:57.780
And now here is the final party planning committee scene with Michael, right?
现在这是最后一场迈克尔参加的派对策划委员会的戏了，对吧？

420
00:19:59.240 --> 00:20:00.480
How about cupcakes?
纸杯蛋糕怎么样？

421
00:20:01.240 --> 00:20:01.760
Please.
求你了。

422
00:20:02.300 --> 00:20:03.480
What's wrong with cupcakes?
纸杯蛋糕有什么不好？

423
00:20:03.740 --> 00:20:03.900
Everything.
哪儿都不好。

424
00:20:04.280 --> 00:20:05.040
There they are.
她们在那儿呢。

425
00:20:05.340 --> 00:20:07.140
Party planning committee together again.
派对策划委员会又聚在一起了。

426
00:20:07.800 --> 00:20:09.780
Well, we all wanted to plan your goodbye party.
嗯，我们都想为你策划欢送派对。

427
00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:11.140
We thought this would be easier.
我们以为这样会简单点。

428
00:20:11.840 --> 00:20:12.600
We thought.
我们以为。

429
00:20:13.540 --> 00:20:15.100
We decided on the ice cream.
我们决定买冰淇淋。

430
00:20:15.340 --> 00:20:16.940
Mint chocolate chip, your favorite.
薄荷巧克力碎，你最喜欢的。

431
00:20:17.380 --> 00:20:17.800
Mmm.
嗯。

432
00:20:18.260 --> 00:20:19.620
Yeah, that was a surprise.
是啊，那是个惊喜。

433
00:20:19.940 --> 00:20:20.420
You know what?
你知道吗？

434
00:20:20.420 --> 00:20:22.840
I'm thinking maybe we should get ice cream that everybody will like.
我在想也许我们应该买大家都喜欢的冰淇淋。

435
00:20:23.180 --> 00:20:24.020
How about vanilla?
香草味怎么样？

436
00:20:24.020 --> 00:20:24.960
Let's get vanilla.
就买香草味的吧。

437
00:20:26.500 --> 00:20:27.140
Okay.
好的。

438
00:20:27.500 --> 00:20:29.760
Tomorrow, I want everybody to have a good time.
明天，我希望大家都能玩得开心。

439
00:20:30.240 --> 00:20:31.300
No drama.
别出什么乱子。

440
00:20:31.720 --> 00:20:34.480
And as for today, just a typical day.
至于今天，就和平常一样。

441
00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:35.640
All right?
好吗？

442
00:20:36.680 --> 00:20:38.000
Should we get toppings?
我们要加配料吗？

443
00:20:38.460 --> 00:20:39.600
What do you like, Pam?
帕姆，你喜欢什么？

444
00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:40.460
What?
什么？

445
00:20:40.700 --> 00:20:42.380
What kind of topping would you like?
你想要什么样的配料？

446
00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:44.300
Topping.
配料。

447
00:20:44.920 --> 00:20:45.860
Sounds good.
听起来不错。

448
00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:47.660
Fudge it up.
多加点软糖酱。

449
00:20:49.700 --> 00:20:55.220
What I love about them is that the dynamic of the party planning committee has not changed.
我喜欢她们的一点是，派对策划委员会的动态一点都没变。

450
00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:55.780
No.
没错。

451
00:20:56.060 --> 00:20:56.220
No.
不。

452
00:20:56.480 --> 00:20:56.660
Yeah.
是啊。

453
00:20:56.940 --> 00:21:01.440
We have grown not at all in our ability to work with one another.
我们在彼此协作的能力上一点长进都没有。

454
00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:02.120
Yeah.
是啊。

455
00:21:02.420 --> 00:21:05.100
I love how surprised you were at being asked your opinion.
我喜欢你被问到意见时那副惊讶的样子。

456
00:21:05.380 --> 00:21:05.620
Yeah.
是啊。

457
00:21:05.860 --> 00:21:07.200
That was such a good read.
那段读起来真棒。

458
00:21:07.900 --> 00:21:08.420
What?
什么？

459
00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:13.240
It's one of those things sometimes where you're afraid it's a trap.
有时候就是这样，你会担心这是个陷阱。

460
00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:13.920
Yeah.
是啊。

461
00:21:13.920 --> 00:21:14.160
Really?
真的吗？

462
00:21:14.240 --> 00:21:14.980
Where is this going?
这要往哪儿发展？

463
00:21:15.200 --> 00:21:15.400
Yeah.
是啊。

464
00:21:15.400 --> 00:21:16.440
I'm sort of scared.
我有点害怕。

465
00:21:16.440 --> 00:21:22.380
Well, I mean, there's another example of slipping in some good exposition there.
嗯，我是说，这又是一个巧妙植入背景信息的例子。

466
00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:25.220
Because he says, like, I don't want any drama today.
因为他说，比如，我今天不想惹任何麻烦。

467
00:21:25.460 --> 00:21:26.620
Just a typical day.
只是平常的一天。

468
00:21:26.820 --> 00:21:31.400
And that's, like, sets up his whole expectation for the episode.
这就像是为他整集的心理预期做了铺垫。

469
00:21:31.400 --> 00:21:36.620
And then, you know, that lets us have an act break out of a very slender thing of, like,
然后，你知道，这让我们能从一个非常细微的点引出幕间休息，比如，

470
00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:38.080
oh, no, I'm not leaving tomorrow.
噢，不，我不是明天走。

471
00:21:38.080 --> 00:21:39.620
I'm leaving today at four or whatever.
我是今天四点走，或者随便什么时候。

472
00:21:39.800 --> 00:21:40.040
Yeah.
是啊。

473
00:21:40.220 --> 00:21:40.360
Yeah.
是啊。

474
00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:40.640
Yeah.
是啊。

475
00:21:40.760 --> 00:21:42.860
I have a slightly cynical question.
我有个稍微有点愤世嫉俗的问题。

476
00:21:43.080 --> 00:21:43.240
Yeah.
是啊。

477
00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:48.760
Do you think Michael would have been more attached to the ice cream flavor if he knew he was going to be at the party?
你觉得如果迈克尔知道自己会参加派对，他还会对冰淇淋口味那么执着吗？

478
00:21:49.140 --> 00:21:49.520
Yes.
会。

479
00:21:49.760 --> 00:21:50.160
I think so.
我也这么觉得。

480
00:21:50.160 --> 00:21:53.800
Is he able to be so generous because he's like, I'm not even going to be there.
他之所以能表现得那么大方，是因为他觉得反正我又不参加。

481
00:21:53.960 --> 00:21:55.200
So whatever you want.
所以你们想怎么样都行。

482
00:21:55.380 --> 00:21:57.100
I don't have to control it if I'm not eating it.
反正我不吃，也就没必要去管它。

483
00:21:57.200 --> 00:21:57.420
Yeah.
是啊。

484
00:21:57.540 --> 00:21:57.940
Exactly.
没错。

485
00:21:58.240 --> 00:21:58.520
Yeah.
是啊。

486
00:21:58.560 --> 00:21:59.060
It's hilarious.
太搞笑了。

487
00:22:00.300 --> 00:22:01.960
Certain amount of growth, but not a ton.
有一定的成长，但不多。

488
00:22:03.140 --> 00:22:10.760
Well, after this scene, Michael's going to have a talking head where he talks about how he bought himself his world's best boss mug.
嗯，在这场戏之后，迈克尔会有一个访谈镜头，讲他给自己买了那个“世界最佳老板”杯子。

489
00:22:10.940 --> 00:22:16.140
But yesterday, the whole office gave him a world's best boss dundee.
但昨天，整个办公室刚送了他一个“世界最佳老板”邓迪奖杯。

490
00:22:16.320 --> 00:22:25.520
So he throws his mug in the trash, and then he sets his dundee on the desk, and it 100% mirrors that opening shot.
于是他把杯子扔进垃圾桶，把邓迪奖杯放在桌上，这百分之百呼应了开头的那个镜头。

491
00:22:25.740 --> 00:22:27.280
How did you guys do that?
你们是怎么做到的？

492
00:22:27.280 --> 00:22:28.300
It's so perfect.
太完美了。

493
00:22:28.520 --> 00:22:29.620
You wouldn't even know.
根本看不出来。

494
00:22:29.740 --> 00:22:31.940
It looks like it's like just copy and paste it in.
看起来就像是直接复制粘贴进去的一样。

495
00:22:32.020 --> 00:22:38.560
I actually paused to see if you tricked us, and you actually cut away to the original shot, but you didn't.
我特意暂停看了看你们是不是在耍我们，以为你们切回了原来的镜头，但并没有。

496
00:22:38.820 --> 00:22:39.660
It's a new shot.
那是新拍的镜头。

497
00:22:39.720 --> 00:22:40.540
It's a new shot.
那是新拍的镜头。

498
00:22:40.680 --> 00:22:40.860
Yeah.
是啊。

499
00:22:41.080 --> 00:22:44.460
Well, that was something that I added to the pilot was that mug.
嗯，那个杯子是我在试播集里加进去的。

500
00:22:44.600 --> 00:22:48.000
The fact that he bought himself his world's best boss mug.
就是他给自己买了那个“世界最佳老板”杯子的设定。

501
00:22:48.980 --> 00:22:55.920
And, you know, when you're doing a pilot, you're always looking for, like, what is the one thing you can do that will encapsulate somebody's...
你知道，在制作试播集时，你总是在寻找那种能概括某人……的东西。

502
00:22:56.340 --> 00:22:56.700
Existence.
存在感。

503
00:22:57.060 --> 00:22:57.420
Yeah.
没错。

504
00:22:57.740 --> 00:23:01.740
His complete psychology in one visual thing, you know.
用一个视觉元素来展现他完整的心理状态，你懂的。

505
00:23:01.740 --> 00:23:09.720
And so I always thought that that prop was, like, a really good, you know, example of somebody who had very little self-knowledge.
所以我一直觉得那个道具是一个很好的例子，体现了一个人对自己缺乏认知。

506
00:23:09.900 --> 00:23:15.580
And so it was good that he kind of outgrew that thing.
所以他能摆脱那种状态是件好事。

507
00:23:15.580 --> 00:23:18.060
And then it was a great episode, the Dundee episode.
那集“邓迪”确实很棒。

508
00:23:18.060 --> 00:23:19.660
The previous one was great.
上一集也很棒。

509
00:23:19.920 --> 00:23:22.480
And I can't remember when.
我不记得是什么时候了。

510
00:23:22.600 --> 00:23:27.620
I think it was just during the writing of it that I realized, like, oh, why don't we see that?
我想是在写剧本的时候，我突然意识到，哎，我们为什么不展示一下那个呢？

511
00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:37.100
Like, the use of documentary little conventions was very sparingly doled out for big moments, right?
比如，纪录片式的拍摄手法通常只在关键时刻才会少量使用，对吧？

512
00:23:37.200 --> 00:23:39.960
So, like, in this one, we pulled out some stops.
所以，在这一集里，我们做了一些特别的尝试。

513
00:23:39.960 --> 00:23:41.360
And we did that.
我们确实那么做了。

514
00:23:41.420 --> 00:23:46.560
And we were like, cool, this is, you know, this is how that first shot came in.
当时我们觉得，酷，这就是那个镜头最初出现的方式。

515
00:23:46.560 --> 00:23:56.660
And, again, like, I think that that has a lot of emotional resonance because you realize, oh, my God, I've been watching that, you know, every week for the whole run of the show.
再说一次，我觉得这很有情感共鸣，因为你会意识到，天哪，我每周都在看这个，贯穿了整部剧。

516
00:23:56.800 --> 00:23:58.600
And this is where it came in, the last episode.
而这正是它出现的地方，在最后一集。

517
00:23:58.800 --> 00:24:00.200
So, like, I thought that was cool.
所以，我觉得这很酷。

518
00:24:00.360 --> 00:24:04.260
But then there's other stuff, like, when he, at the end, when he takes his mic off and stuff like that.
但还有其他东西，比如最后他摘下麦克风的时候之类的。

519
00:24:04.360 --> 00:24:10.420
And I feel like the taking the mic off was a big moment in the English show, I think.
我觉得摘麦克风在英版剧集中是一个重大的时刻。

520
00:24:10.580 --> 00:24:11.020
It was.
确实是。

521
00:24:11.140 --> 00:24:16.360
There's a moment when Tim takes his microphone off when he's going to tell his feelings to Don.
蒂姆在准备向唐表露心迹时，有一个摘下麦克风的镜头。

522
00:24:16.560 --> 00:24:16.660
Yeah.
没错。

523
00:24:17.060 --> 00:24:20.080
And I think it's even in the Christmas special, if I'm correct.
如果我没记错的话，那应该是在圣诞特辑里。

524
00:24:20.360 --> 00:24:24.380
So, that was obviously, that's like a silver bullet that you get to use once.
所以，那显然是一张王牌，你只能用一次。

525
00:24:24.720 --> 00:24:24.860
Yeah.
没错。

526
00:24:24.980 --> 00:24:26.040
And we saved it for this.
我们把它留到了这一集。

527
00:24:26.600 --> 00:24:29.980
Well, Michael is going to take out a list of employees' names.
迈克尔要拿出一份员工名单。

528
00:24:30.060 --> 00:24:33.820
And you can see the list at five minutes and 32 seconds.
你可以在5分32秒的时候看到那份名单。

529
00:24:34.440 --> 00:24:37.660
And, Greg, did that list sort of shape the episode for you?
格雷格，那份名单对这一集的构思有影响吗？

530
00:24:37.860 --> 00:24:39.220
Did you have an outline with that?
你当时有大纲吗？

531
00:24:40.160 --> 00:24:42.420
Well, let me just remember this little story.
嗯，让我回忆一下那个小故事。

532
00:24:42.540 --> 00:24:47.100
Because I used to work on a show called The Wilton North Report.
因为我以前在一家叫《威尔顿北方报道》的节目组工作过。

533
00:24:47.820 --> 00:24:50.000
And Conan and I both worked there.
柯南和我也都在那里工作。

534
00:24:51.020 --> 00:24:56.740
It was a weird brief experience of a late night variety show.
那是一档深夜综艺节目，虽然经历很短暂且奇怪。

535
00:24:56.740 --> 00:25:01.380
And they did have a cool documentary collective that was part of that show.
他们确实有一个很酷的纪录片团队参与了节目制作。

536
00:25:01.560 --> 00:25:12.340
And one thing I did once was take this documentary crew and go to this guy's retirement party who was retiring from the gas company, SoCal Gas.
有一次我带着纪录片摄制组去参加了一个人的退休派对，他是南加州天然气公司的员工。

537
00:25:12.340 --> 00:25:22.780
And we just shot it and kind of looked for something that would be touching or humorous about just sort of this average guy retiring from the gas company.
我们只是拍摄并寻找一些关于这个普通人从天然气公司退休的感人或幽默的瞬间。

538
00:25:23.140 --> 00:25:29.600
And anyway, the mood of that informs this script for me.
总之，那种氛围为我撰写这个剧本提供了灵感。

539
00:25:29.640 --> 00:25:34.620
Because that guy was being toasted by people he'd worked with for a really long time.
因为那个人正在接受与他共事很久的同事们的祝酒。

540
00:25:34.620 --> 00:25:35.680
He was leaving.
他要离开了。

541
00:25:35.900 --> 00:25:36.920
They gave him little gifts.
他们送了他一些小礼物。

542
00:25:37.360 --> 00:25:39.200
You know, like, here's a golf ball.
你知道，比如，这是一个高尔夫球。

543
00:25:39.300 --> 00:25:41.200
You can use it on your golf or whatever, you know.
你可以打高尔夫的时候用，或者随便什么，你懂的。

544
00:25:41.400 --> 00:25:42.820
But it was almost sad.
但这几乎让人感到悲伤。

545
00:25:42.940 --> 00:25:49.140
It was very sad because he was – they were almost packing him on a Viking ship and lighting him on fire and sending him off.
真的很悲伤，因为他们简直就像是把他送上一艘维京海盗船，点火烧掉，然后送他远行。

546
00:25:49.860 --> 00:25:53.580
It was like I don't think he was going to see any of these people again, you know.
感觉他以后再也不会见到这些人了，你懂的。

547
00:25:53.700 --> 00:25:55.680
And it was very bittersweet.
那种感觉非常苦乐参半。

548
00:25:56.100 --> 00:25:58.760
And so, I mean, I had that mood in the back of my head.
所以，我的脑海里一直萦绕着那种情绪。

549
00:25:59.120 --> 00:26:01.380
And then when Michael got the list, he was going to go.
然后当迈克尔拿到名单时，他就要走了。

550
00:26:01.380 --> 00:26:08.580
Well, the thing about the list was it was kind of like the structure of the episode is he's going to say his goodbyes.
关于那份名单，其实它构成了这一集的结构，因为他要开始告别了。

551
00:26:09.740 --> 00:26:13.860
And so, the list was a good roadmap for where we were going to go.
所以，这份名单为我们接下来的走向提供了一份很好的路线图。

552
00:26:14.000 --> 00:26:17.260
And so, once you saw the list, you were like, okay, I know how this episode is going to go.
所以，一旦你看到了这份名单，你就会想，好吧，我知道这一集会怎么发展了。

553
00:26:17.360 --> 00:26:21.280
I have a general feeling that he's going to have to cross off everybody on the liSt.
我有一种预感，他最终得把名单上的每个人都划掉。

554
00:26:21.280 --> 00:26:28.700
And considering that the big sort of dilemma that he has at the end is he hasn't gotten to Pam, you know,
考虑到他最后面临的最大困境是他还没找帕姆，你知道的，

555
00:26:28.800 --> 00:26:34.860
to visually see the list and see everybody get crossed off except Pam is going to be our structure.
能直观地看到这份名单，看到除了帕姆之外的所有人都被划掉，这将成为我们的叙事结构。

556
00:26:35.540 --> 00:26:37.480
So, that was very useful to have the liSt.
所以，有这份名单真的很有用。

557
00:26:38.040 --> 00:26:41.460
It definitely reminded me of the Wizard of Oz a little bit.
它确实让我想起了一点《绿野仙踪》的感觉。

558
00:26:41.580 --> 00:26:43.260
Yeah, there's a lot of Wizard of Oz in this.
没错，这一集里确实有很多《绿野仙踪》的影子。

559
00:26:43.480 --> 00:26:43.660
Yeah.
是啊。

560
00:26:43.660 --> 00:26:51.880
Yeah, like, you know, it's like that final scene when they meet with the great Oz and he's like, you get a diploma and you get a medal.
对，就像最后他们见到伟大的奥兹那一幕，他说，你得到一个文凭，你得到一枚奖章。

561
00:26:52.100 --> 00:26:55.600
It's like Phyllis is shy and doesn't, you know, speak up for herself.
就像菲利斯很害羞，你知道的，不为自己争取。

562
00:26:55.720 --> 00:26:57.260
She gets the clattering teeth.
她得到的是一副会咔哒作响的假牙。

563
00:26:57.480 --> 00:26:58.800
Yeah, totally.
没错，完全是这样。

564
00:26:59.060 --> 00:27:05.900
And I think he watched Wizard of Oz and saw himself as the Wizard of Oz maybe on some level.
而且我觉得他可能看了《绿野仙踪》，在某种程度上把自己看作了奥兹巫师。

565
00:27:05.900 --> 00:27:15.700
Yeah, I did catch a moment where I saw some real Michael growth because when he gives Stanley like the novelty pool table, Stanley says, it's got no balls.
是啊，我确实捕捉到了一个瞬间，看到了迈克尔真正的成长，因为当他送给斯坦利那个新奇的台球桌时，斯坦利说，这上面没有球。

566
00:27:15.800 --> 00:27:17.520
And Michael doesn't say anything.
而迈克尔什么也没说。

567
00:27:17.800 --> 00:27:19.260
Yes, I noticed that too.
是的，我也注意到了。

568
00:27:19.400 --> 00:27:20.240
He would have said that's what she said.
他本来会说“那是她说的”的。

569
00:27:20.500 --> 00:27:20.680
Yeah.
是啊。

570
00:27:21.080 --> 00:27:30.660
Well, also, I think the funny, that's also setting up this subplot in this episode is that Stanley got this little broken toy.
嗯，而且我觉得有趣的是，这也为这一集的副线剧情做了铺垫，就是斯坦利得到了这个破损的小玩具。

571
00:27:30.660 --> 00:27:35.120
Toy, and then Andy gets the 10 biggest clients right afterwards.
玩具，然后紧接着安迪就得到了那10个大客户。

572
00:27:35.440 --> 00:27:36.260
And he's like, I'm going to lose them.
然后他说，我要失去他们了。

573
00:27:36.440 --> 00:27:37.300
I'm going to lose them.
我要失去他们了。

574
00:27:37.380 --> 00:27:39.040
And then Michael's like, I have faith in you.
然后迈克尔说，我相信你。

575
00:27:39.240 --> 00:27:43.160
And then later he shouts out in the middle of the scene, I just lost one.
后来他在场景中间大喊，我刚丢了一个。

576
00:27:43.520 --> 00:27:43.940
I just lost one.
我刚丢了一个。

577
00:27:44.020 --> 00:27:44.100
Border hardware.
边境五金公司。

578
00:27:44.360 --> 00:27:45.600
I just lost border hardware, Michael.
我刚丢了边境五金公司，迈克尔。

579
00:27:46.120 --> 00:27:46.480
Yes.
是的。

580
00:27:47.520 --> 00:27:47.860
Yeah.
是啊。

581
00:27:48.580 --> 00:27:49.580
No, I love that.
不，我喜欢这个。

582
00:27:49.660 --> 00:27:53.840
That was really, like, I was confident that was going to be a big laugh in writing it.
这真的很棒，在写剧本的时候我就确信这会是一个很大的笑点。

583
00:27:53.880 --> 00:27:55.940
I was like, I have him yell from across, you know.
我当时想，让他从对面喊出来，你知道的。

584
00:27:56.280 --> 00:28:00.140
I also, I loved it on the show when there were stuff coming off Mike.
我也很喜欢剧里那些从迈克那边传过来的声音。

585
00:28:00.140 --> 00:28:01.200
You know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

586
00:28:01.200 --> 00:28:03.180
It just felt so real.
这感觉太真实了。

587
00:28:03.320 --> 00:28:05.380
But you're just like, oh, we're over here in accounting.
但你就会想，哦，我们现在在会计部这边。

588
00:28:05.540 --> 00:28:05.820
Oh, no.
哦，不。

589
00:28:06.600 --> 00:28:09.720
He's going to lob this joke in from his B-plot.
他又要从他的副线剧情里抛出这个笑话了。

590
00:28:10.140 --> 00:28:10.700
All right.
好的。

591
00:28:10.800 --> 00:28:12.380
I think we should take a break.
我想我们该休息一下了。

592
00:28:12.480 --> 00:28:15.240
And when we come back, keep breaking down the episode.
等我们回来，继续解析这一集。

593
00:28:15.540 --> 00:28:15.880
Like it.
喜欢这个提议。

594
00:28:25.150 --> 00:28:27.590
We are back and we are still in accounting.
我们回来了，依然在会计部。

595
00:28:28.430 --> 00:28:32.470
Michael presents Kevin with a drawing of Kevin as a pig eating pizza.
迈克尔送给凯文一幅画，画的是凯文变成了一头吃披萨的猪。

596
00:28:32.870 --> 00:28:38.050
But then he tears up the picture and he says, don't be a caricature, Kevin.
但随后他把画撕了，说，别活成个漫画人物，凯文。

597
00:28:38.630 --> 00:28:43.130
That's his gift to Kevin, I guess, is this, what, this lesson?
我想这就是他送给凯文的礼物，这个，什么，这个教训？

598
00:28:43.750 --> 00:28:47.010
Well, and Kevin says, I kind of am, like, good with myself.
嗯，凯文说，我对自己挺满意的。

599
00:28:47.010 --> 00:28:47.950
I like who I am.
我喜欢现在的自己。

600
00:28:48.010 --> 00:28:50.410
And Michael says, never settle for who you are.
而迈克尔说，永远不要满足于现在的自己。

601
00:28:51.570 --> 00:28:52.030
Yeah.
是啊。

602
00:28:52.230 --> 00:28:56.910
So that's maybe more old-fashioned Michael giving some bad lessons out.
所以那可能更多是老派的迈克尔在传授一些错误的经验。

603
00:28:56.910 --> 00:28:58.730
But, I mean, I always did.
但我意思是，我一直都是这么做的。

