746
00:35:50.490 --> 00:35:54.890
I feel like you had one comment about his aide earlier.
我觉得你之前好像评论过他的助手。

747
00:35:55.330 --> 00:35:55.590
Yes.
是的。

748
00:35:55.810 --> 00:35:55.910
No.
没有。

749
00:35:56.190 --> 00:35:58.470
Didn't he join you for Valentine's Day or something?
他不是情人节那天和你一起参加活动还是什么的吗？

750
00:35:58.650 --> 00:35:58.950
Yes.
是的。

751
00:35:59.150 --> 00:35:59.450
Yes.
是的。

752
00:35:59.450 --> 00:36:05.950
Actually, it might have been in deleted scenes, but I shared it that everyone talks about how they're going to spend their Valentine's Day.
其实，那段可能是在删减片段里，但我分享过大家都在讨论情人节打算怎么过的内容。

753
00:36:06.190 --> 00:36:09.750
And Angela has a talking head where she was like, the senator's taking me out somewhere.
安吉拉有个采访镜头，她说参议员要带她去什么地方。

754
00:36:09.830 --> 00:36:12.470
But then he has to leave early to meet his aide, Thomas.
但后来他得早走去见他的助手托马斯。

755
00:36:12.770 --> 00:36:13.290
To do a little work.
去处理点工作。

756
00:36:13.370 --> 00:36:15.610
They do a lot of late-night work sessions.
他们经常有深夜工作会议。

757
00:36:15.850 --> 00:36:16.010
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

758
00:36:16.410 --> 00:36:16.630
Yes.
是的。

759
00:36:17.130 --> 00:36:20.130
Well, Randy shared with us that these pictures were not shot on a green screen.
兰迪跟我们分享过，这些照片并不是在绿幕前拍的。

760
00:36:20.130 --> 00:36:26.770
You actually went to an antique shop, and you went to a nearby street to go rollerblading to shoot those photos.
你们真的去了古董店，还去了附近的街道滑旱冰来拍那些照片。

761
00:36:27.310 --> 00:36:28.230
Do you remember that, Ange?
安吉，你还记得吗？

762
00:36:28.310 --> 00:36:28.590
I do.
我记得。

763
00:36:28.690 --> 00:36:31.350
We sort of did it all in one day, and we drove to a few different places.
我们基本上是一天之内搞定的，开车去了好几个不同的地方。

764
00:36:31.350 --> 00:36:35.350
And I was most excited about rollerblading because I love to roller skate.
我最兴奋的就是滑旱冰，因为我特别喜欢溜冰。

765
00:36:35.550 --> 00:36:40.250
And so I was very excited that my character got to do anything other than just sit in a corner and scowl.
所以我很高兴我的角色终于能做点除了坐在角落里皱眉头以外的事了。

766
00:36:40.410 --> 00:36:42.790
But rollerblading is very different than roller skating.
但滑旱冰和溜冰其实很不一样。

767
00:36:42.790 --> 00:36:43.150
It is.
确实。

768
00:36:43.150 --> 00:36:43.910
Can you do both?
你两种都会吗？

769
00:36:44.050 --> 00:36:44.870
I can do both.
我两种都会。

770
00:36:44.870 --> 00:36:46.290
I prefer roller skating.
我更喜欢溜冰。

771
00:36:46.690 --> 00:36:51.610
But I was just excited to be outside and skate, and I got to wear shorts.
但我当时只是很兴奋能到户外去滑，而且我还能穿短裤。

772
00:36:51.830 --> 00:36:55.470
And I got a day where I got to travel around the valley.
那天我还有机会在山谷里到处转转。

773
00:36:56.330 --> 00:36:57.550
Antiquing and rollerblading.
逛古董店和滑旱冰。

774
00:36:57.790 --> 00:36:58.110
Antiquing and rollerblading.
逛古董店和滑旱冰。

775
00:36:58.250 --> 00:36:59.130
It was really fun.
真的很有趣。

776
00:36:59.430 --> 00:36:59.890
Nice.
不错。

777
00:37:00.230 --> 00:37:09.350
So we have failed to mention D'Angelo's struggle in this episode, which is that he is being very tempted by all the snacks in the vending machine.
我们还没提到这一集里迪安杰洛的挣扎，就是他被自动售货机里的各种零食诱惑得不行。

778
00:37:09.610 --> 00:37:11.610
We're going to see him in the break room now.
我们现在要去休息室看看他。

779
00:37:11.610 --> 00:37:16.150
And he is making a s'more on the heating pad of the coffee maker.
他正在咖啡机的加热垫上做烤棉花糖夹心饼干。

780
00:37:17.410 --> 00:37:21.450
And Andy is going to come in and say he needs some help with a client.
安迪一会儿会进来，说他需要帮忙处理一个客户。

781
00:37:21.990 --> 00:37:22.890
Greg, have you done this?
格雷格，你做过这种事吗？

782
00:37:23.030 --> 00:37:25.670
Have you made a s'more, like, in a microwave or something?
比如用微波炉或者什么东西做过烤棉花糖夹心饼干？

783
00:37:25.750 --> 00:37:27.110
I feel like this is something you would do.
我觉得这像是你会做的事。

784
00:37:27.110 --> 00:37:33.170
Because I have been in the kitchen with you where you're like, we only had a few ingredients of something, and maybe we didn't have all the right utensils.
因为我和你在厨房待过，当时你说，我们只有几种配料，可能也没有合适的餐具。

785
00:37:33.250 --> 00:37:34.410
You're like, let's try it.
你就说，咱们试试吧。

786
00:37:34.410 --> 00:37:43.010
Well, I went to boarding school, and so a lot of times, you know, if you couldn't cook, you had no access to the kitchen.
我上过寄宿学校，很多时候，如果你不会做饭，又没法进厨房。

787
00:37:43.370 --> 00:37:49.650
And so sometimes you have to, like, make up stuff that you could do with one of those little coils that heats up.
所以有时候你不得不利用那种加热线圈来搞点发明创造。

788
00:37:49.950 --> 00:37:50.350
Yeah.
没错。

789
00:37:50.590 --> 00:37:52.030
You know, so if there was any –
你知道，所以如果有任何——

790
00:37:52.030 --> 00:37:54.170
Grilled cheese with an iron, that sort of thing.
用熨斗做烤芝士三明治，就是那种事。

791
00:37:54.170 --> 00:37:54.950
Yeah, that kind of thing.
对，就是那种。

792
00:37:54.950 --> 00:37:57.810
Well, we had a fan catch from Madison M.
我们收到了来自科罗拉多州丹佛市麦迪逊·M的粉丝发现，在这一集里，我得先说一句，麦迪逊是对的。

793
00:37:57.910 --> 00:38:03.530
in Denver, Colorado in this episode, and I'm going to just say ahead of time, Madison is correct.
麦迪逊说，我注意到了这一集里的一个连贯性错误。

794
00:38:04.370 --> 00:38:07.370
Madison said, I noticed a continuity error in this episode.
在10分40秒时，迪安杰洛正在用咖啡壶做棉花糖巧克力点心。

795
00:38:07.530 --> 00:38:12.070
At 10 minutes and 40 seconds, D'Angelo is cooking the marshmallow chocolate treat with the coffee pot.
安迪走进来，在10分51秒时，他用左手把它扔进了垃圾桶。

796
00:38:12.250 --> 00:38:18.150
Andy walks in, and at 10 minutes and 51 seconds, he throws it in the garbage with his left hand.
但在11分钟时，当他拍打门框上方并留下巧克力指纹时，用的是右手。

797
00:38:18.790 --> 00:38:24.630
But at 11 minutes, when he slaps the top of the doorway and leaves chocolate fingerprints, it's with his right hand.
真是个不错的发现。

798
00:38:26.490 --> 00:38:27.190
That's a nice catch.
发现得真好。

799
00:38:27.270 --> 00:38:27.650
That's a good catch.
是的。

800
00:38:27.950 --> 00:38:28.130
Yeah.
没错。

801
00:38:28.350 --> 00:38:32.970
I mean, it's possible he had chocolate all over himself, but that's a good catch.
我是说，他身上沾满巧克力是有可能的，但你观察得真仔细。

802
00:38:33.150 --> 00:38:38.150
I remember that chocolate fingerprint hand being up there for a very long time.
我记得那个巧克力指纹手印在那儿待了很久。

803
00:38:38.630 --> 00:38:42.910
I'm eager now to watch it and try to spot it every time.
我现在很想回去看一遍，试着每次都把它找出来。

804
00:38:43.090 --> 00:38:44.190
When was it ever cleaned off?
它到底是什么时候被清理掉的？

805
00:38:44.290 --> 00:38:45.430
I don't know if it ever was.
我不知道它有没有被清理过。

806
00:38:45.590 --> 00:38:47.050
I mean, it might be there till the end.
我是说，它可能一直都在那儿，直到最后。

807
00:38:47.330 --> 00:38:53.150
I don't know, but I feel like it's definitely above my head when I'm doing the fake juggling in the break room
我不知道，但我感觉当我做那个假杂耍的时候，它肯定就在我头顶上方，就在休息室里，

808
00:38:53.810 --> 00:38:55.850
in D'Angelo's last episode.
在迪安杰洛的最后一集里。

809
00:38:56.090 --> 00:38:57.730
Can I tell a quick story about The Simpsons?
我能讲个关于《辛普森一家》的短故事吗？

810
00:38:58.210 --> 00:38:59.230
Yes, please.
好啊，请讲。

811
00:38:59.430 --> 00:39:02.470
No, nobody wants stories about The Simpsons.
不，没人想听关于《辛普森一家》的故事。

812
00:39:03.430 --> 00:39:07.110
When I joined the writing staff on The Simpsons, which was the end of season four,
当我加入《辛普森一家》编剧组时，那是第四季末尾，

813
00:39:08.150 --> 00:39:16.230
in the writer's room, there was this weird brown object stuck to the ceiling.
在编剧室的天花板上粘着一个奇怪的棕色物体。

814
00:39:16.690 --> 00:39:24.850
And it turned out that somebody had chewed up a bunch of caramels, stuck it on a doll of Bart,
后来发现是有人嚼了一堆焦糖，把它粘在一个巴特玩偶上，

815
00:39:25.110 --> 00:39:28.030
on his spiky hair, and stuck him to the ceiling.
粘在他那尖尖的头发上，然后把他贴到了天花板上。

816
00:39:28.490 --> 00:39:31.330
And then that was like a little room bit for a while.
那段时间这成了房间里的一个小梗。

817
00:39:31.330 --> 00:39:34.930
And then the doll fell off, and the caramels were there.
后来玩偶掉了下来，但焦糖还留在上面。

818
00:39:35.070 --> 00:39:37.290
And this was like two years old by the time I got there.
等我到那儿的时候，这东西都已经在那儿两年了。

819
00:39:37.370 --> 00:39:39.810
And they were like, oh, yes, I'll tell you the story about the caramels in the ceiling.
他们当时说，哦，对了，我给你讲讲天花板上焦糖的故事。

820
00:39:40.090 --> 00:39:40.830
It's just hard.
这事儿挺难办的。

821
00:39:40.990 --> 00:39:42.770
And I was like, yeah, why doesn't anybody clean it up?
我就问，是啊，为什么没人把它清理掉呢？

822
00:39:43.270 --> 00:39:46.190
But, yeah, those kind of things will last sometimes in an office.
不过，是啊，这种东西在办公室里有时确实会留很久。

823
00:39:46.390 --> 00:39:49.610
Like the chocolate fingerprints could be there two years later.
就像那个巧克力指纹，两年后可能还在那儿。

824
00:39:49.790 --> 00:39:51.310
People are like, oh, yeah, that was the time that it was.
大家会说，哦，对，就是那次留下的。

825
00:39:51.310 --> 00:39:51.610
Yeah.
是啊。

826
00:39:52.810 --> 00:39:53.810
It just lives there now.
它现在就成了那儿的一部分了。

827
00:39:53.850 --> 00:39:55.410
I feel like I have those things in my house.
我觉得我家里也有这种东西。

828
00:39:55.410 --> 00:39:57.710
I feel like I'm like, oh, yeah, that was a kid's.
我感觉就像是，哦，对，那是孩子留下的。

829
00:39:57.790 --> 00:39:59.650
You become blind to stuff in your house.
你会对家里的东西视而不见。

830
00:39:59.650 --> 00:40:03.150
No, I mean, like, I feel like we have, like, here's a perfect example.
不，我是说，我觉得我们有，比如，这儿有个完美的例子。

831
00:40:03.450 --> 00:40:09.150
One year for Halloween, we put, like, handprints and footprints on the gate, you know, the side gate of our house.
有一年万圣节，我们在大门上，就是我们家侧门，贴了手印和脚印，你知道的。

832
00:40:09.270 --> 00:40:09.490
Okay.
好的。

833
00:40:09.750 --> 00:40:12.470
They were like a path, you know, like a scary path.
它们就像一条路，你知道，一条恐怖小径。

834
00:40:12.610 --> 00:40:14.870
And when we peeled them off, part of them remained.
当我们把它们撕下来时，有一部分还留着。

835
00:40:15.070 --> 00:40:18.050
They didn't peel off exactly, and, like, part of the sticky's there.
它们没能完全撕下来，胶印还留在那儿。

836
00:40:18.190 --> 00:40:18.530
Oh, I see.
哦，我明白了。

837
00:40:18.530 --> 00:40:19.690
And now they just live there.
现在它们就一直待在那儿了。

838
00:40:19.870 --> 00:40:20.050
Yeah.
是啊。

839
00:40:20.490 --> 00:40:23.530
You get completely blind to the stuff in your environment.
你会对周围环境里的东西完全视而不见。

840
00:40:23.530 --> 00:40:31.770
Like, I'm sure that somewhere in my house there's a list of things that a dog who died, like, six years ago can't eat or whatever.
就像我肯定我家里某处还贴着一张清单，上面写着那只六年前去世的狗不能吃什么之类的东西。

841
00:40:32.010 --> 00:40:33.470
It's just still in the kitchen.
它就还在厨房里。

842
00:40:33.650 --> 00:40:34.450
It's taped up.
贴在墙上。

843
00:40:34.570 --> 00:40:37.790
Do not feed this dog who no longer is with us.
不要喂这只已经不在我们身边的狗。

844
00:40:38.190 --> 00:40:38.890
No chicken.
不能吃鸡肉。

845
00:40:39.170 --> 00:40:50.870
The worst thing you can do is get out a magic eraser and start, like, erasering part of some handprints on your wall because then all you see is, like, how smudgy your walls are.
最糟糕的事情就是你拿出魔力擦，开始擦墙上的手印，因为那样你只会看到你的墙有多脏。

846
00:40:50.870 --> 00:40:52.690
Yeah, that's life with kids.
是啊，这就是有孩子的生活。

847
00:40:52.910 --> 00:40:54.530
Yeah, that's a hole I went down recently.
是啊，我最近就陷入了这个怪圈。

848
00:40:55.210 --> 00:40:59.310
Well, Oscar is going to ask Michael where he should send his last paycheck.
好吧，奥斯卡要问迈克尔他的最后一张工资支票该寄到哪儿。

849
00:41:00.190 --> 00:41:01.950
And everything hits Michael.
而迈克尔对此毫无头绪。

850
00:41:02.470 --> 00:41:04.070
He doesn't even know his address.
他甚至不知道自己的地址。

851
00:41:04.390 --> 00:41:04.440
It's real.
这是真的。

852
00:41:04.610 --> 00:41:04.870
Yeah.
是啊。

853
00:41:04.870 --> 00:41:05.970
He said, I don't know.
他说，我不知道。

854
00:41:06.050 --> 00:41:10.230
I live in Mountain Tun, you know, and he starts to freak out.
我说我住在山屯，你知道的，然后他就开始抓狂了。

855
00:41:10.450 --> 00:41:16.670
And then he goes into the break room, and everyone is just hanging out and just eating and having a normal day.
接着他走进休息室，大家都在那儿闲聊、吃东西，过着平常的一天。

856
00:41:16.810 --> 00:41:20.050
And he's sitting in the corner, and he's just becoming more and more emotional.
他坐在角落里，情绪变得越来越激动。

857
00:41:20.050 --> 00:41:25.450
Yeah, Pam's talking about how she's going to have to buy a new shredder because the last one broke.
是啊，帕姆在说她得买台新碎纸机，因为旧的那台坏了。

858
00:41:26.030 --> 00:41:29.550
I love it that Kevin's like, buy one that shreds magazines.
我特别喜欢凯文说的那句，买台能碎杂志的。

859
00:41:29.870 --> 00:41:32.130
Yeah, why is he so fixated on shredding magazines?
是啊，他为什么那么执着于碎杂志？

860
00:41:32.210 --> 00:41:32.810
I don't know.
我不知道。

861
00:41:33.090 --> 00:41:33.830
He clearly broke the shredder.
显然是他把碎纸机弄坏了。

862
00:41:33.850 --> 00:41:34.370
I know.
我知道。

863
00:41:34.490 --> 00:41:37.190
She's like, Kevin, none of them shred magazines.
帕姆就说，凯文，没哪台碎纸机能碎杂志。

864
00:41:37.470 --> 00:41:40.830
And then Jim is like, Kevin, did you break the last shredder?
然后吉姆就问，凯文，是不是你弄坏了上一台碎纸机？

865
00:41:42.010 --> 00:41:45.490
These are such like real fly-on-the-wall office conversations.
这些对话听起来就像办公室里真实的偷听片段。

866
00:41:45.490 --> 00:41:46.650
I feel like I love them.
我觉得我超爱这些对话。

867
00:41:46.810 --> 00:41:56.670
Well, that's what I loved also about this episode is he's leaving, and there's so much opportunity for really mundane moments to hit him emotionally.
嗯，这也是我喜欢这一集的原因，他要走了，那些平凡的瞬间对他而言都变得感伤起来。

868
00:41:57.090 --> 00:42:05.690
Like at the very, very end when he looks back, and it's just, you know, the typical sounds of the office is he's about to leave, and he's the only one who knows he's leaving.
就像最后他回头看的时候，在他即将离开时，办公室里传来了熟悉的声音，而他是唯一一个知道自己要走的人。

869
00:42:05.890 --> 00:42:14.470
But this is another one of those moments where he's just overhearing this chitter-chatter, and yet it's also setting up Pam's lie that's going to get her out of the office later.
但这又是那种他无意中听到闲聊的时刻，同时也为帕姆后来离开办公室所编的谎言做了铺垫。

870
00:42:14.470 --> 00:42:16.430
Yeah, but it's so true.
是啊，太真实了。

871
00:42:16.450 --> 00:42:24.690
When you have to say goodbye to something that means a lot to you, I even remember, you know, when we were writing our book, and I went back, and I re-watched the finale,
当你不得不向对自己意义重大的事物告别时，我甚至记得，我们在写书的时候，我回去重看了大结局，

872
00:42:24.910 --> 00:42:29.570
and kind of reliving that last week, and everything became big.
重温了最后那一周，一切都变得意义非凡。

873
00:42:29.710 --> 00:42:31.750
I'm like, this is the last hot snack.
我当时想，这是最后一次吃热食了。

874
00:42:32.210 --> 00:42:32.530
Yeah.
是啊。

875
00:42:32.710 --> 00:42:35.470
Last time I'm going to have, you know, hot dogs at 1030.
这是我最后一次在十点半吃热狗了。

876
00:42:35.610 --> 00:42:38.090
This is the last time I'm going to be freezing on this set.
这是我最后一次在这个片场挨冻了。

877
00:42:38.230 --> 00:42:41.490
Do you remember the gift that I made for Steve when he left?
你还记得史蒂夫离开时我送他的礼物吗？

878
00:42:41.490 --> 00:42:52.110
So, basically, I went and I saw three places that he did a lot of work from, and I took very high-quality photos of what he would see.
基本上，我去了三个他工作最多的地方，拍下了他平时会看到的景象的高清照片。

879
00:42:52.350 --> 00:42:52.970
His view.
他的视角。

880
00:42:53.090 --> 00:42:56.730
His view of the crew and the other caSt.
他看剧组和其他演员的视角。

881
00:42:56.870 --> 00:42:59.350
So, I had one from him behind his desk.
所以我拍了一张他坐在办公桌后的视角。

882
00:43:00.450 --> 00:43:01.250
POV, yeah.
第一人称视角，没错。

883
00:43:01.250 --> 00:43:11.410
His POV, and I put, like, all the, you know, I put Veda sitting there with her notebook and the cameras and, you know, so that it was like a reminder of what he used to see.
他的第一人称视角，我把维达坐在那儿拿着笔记本、摄像机什么的都放进去了，这样就像是他曾经看到的景象的纪念。

884
00:43:11.490 --> 00:43:13.290
When he looked up from his filming.
当他从拍摄中抬头看的时候。

885
00:43:13.510 --> 00:43:18.510
And then I did one of all you guys in the conference room, what he saw when he was standing in front of the conference room.
然后我拍了一张你们在会议室里的照片，就是他站在会议室前看到的景象。

886
00:43:18.610 --> 00:43:23.190
And I think there was one other one in the bigger room that had a lot of the crew in it.
我想在那个大房间里还有一张，里面有很多剧组成员。

887
00:43:23.350 --> 00:43:23.490
Yeah.
是啊。

888
00:43:23.950 --> 00:43:27.790
Just so he could remember what his point of view was of those things.
就是为了让他能记住自己看这些东西时的视角。

889
00:43:27.910 --> 00:43:30.430
But it's sort of the same thing a little bit emotionally here.
但这在情感上其实有点相似。

890
00:43:30.590 --> 00:43:35.910
It's like, here he is sitting and he's just looking out at, you know, an average scene from that.
就像他现在坐在这里，看着那份工作中平凡的一幕。

891
00:43:35.910 --> 00:43:36.730
Yeah.
是啊。

892
00:43:37.250 --> 00:43:37.630
Job.
工作。

893
00:43:38.190 --> 00:43:40.410
And those are the ones that hit you so hard.
而这些瞬间最让人感触深刻。

894
00:43:41.010 --> 00:43:44.270
Well, he's going to go into his office now and he's like, I can't do this.
好吧，他现在要回办公室了，他说，我做不到。

895
00:43:44.350 --> 00:43:45.150
I can't do this.
我做不到。

896
00:43:45.410 --> 00:43:48.830
And he's starting to freak out about moving and he's going to call Holly.
他开始为搬家感到抓狂，准备给霍莉打电话。

897
00:43:49.250 --> 00:43:56.290
Before he does, he has my favorite line in the episode, which is, I'm not going to start improv at level one.
在那之前，他说了我这集里最喜欢的一句台词：我可不想从即兴表演一级开始。

898
00:43:56.450 --> 00:43:58.630
I don't think my credits are going to transfer.
我觉得我的学分应该转不过去。

899
00:43:59.470 --> 00:44:03.550
If you've taken an improv class, you guys, there are so many levels.
如果你们上过即兴表演课，就会知道，那里面有很多等级。

900
00:44:03.810 --> 00:44:09.010
And if you have to repeat a level for whatever reason, there's like eight levels sometimes.
如果因为某种原因你不得不重修一级，有时候总共有八个等级呢。

901
00:44:09.490 --> 00:44:10.970
And that just got me.
那真的触动了我。

902
00:44:11.090 --> 00:44:12.350
I've said it many times.
我讲过很多次了。

903
00:44:12.550 --> 00:44:20.290
So the thing I think is so brilliant about Steve is his ability to play multiple things going on in his head at the same time.
我觉得史蒂夫最厉害的地方在于，他能同时处理脑海中涌现出的多种想法。

904
00:44:20.450 --> 00:44:22.010
And I love the speech.
我特别喜欢那段演讲。

905
00:44:22.150 --> 00:44:22.650
It's so funny.
太搞笑了。

906
00:44:22.770 --> 00:44:24.450
Everything is really funny in the speech.
演讲里的每一处都特别好笑。

907
00:44:24.450 --> 00:44:28.170
It's just so unexpected that he's worrying about his improv credits at this point.
他竟然在这种时候还在担心自己的即兴表演学分，真是太出人意料了。

908
00:44:29.610 --> 00:44:32.670
I don't think we've thought about him being an improv class in years.
我想我们好几年都没想过他还在上即兴表演课这回事了。

909
00:44:33.810 --> 00:44:36.750
I love to think that he's been in it all along.
我喜欢想象他其实一直都在上课。

910
00:44:36.970 --> 00:44:37.150
Yeah.
是啊。

911
00:44:37.330 --> 00:44:37.590
Yeah.
没错。

912
00:44:37.870 --> 00:44:40.010
This is like a greatest hits episode to me.
对我来说，这集就像是精选集。

913
00:44:40.170 --> 00:44:41.330
It's like this is, you know,
就像是，你知道的，

914
00:44:41.590 --> 00:44:51.930
that was one of the reasons why I was so happy to be able to write it because I have memories of every episode going up to here with him from the pilot to this episode and making little references to it.
这也是我很高兴能参与编剧的原因之一，因为从试播集到这一集，我和他一起走过的每一集记忆都历历在目，能把这些小细节串联起来。

915
00:44:51.930 --> 00:44:59.410
Like that was such a brilliant Gents a lot of written episode, the one where he's doing improv and he invents Michael Scarn.
比如那集他做即兴表演并创造出迈克尔·斯卡恩的那集，写得真是太精彩了。

916
00:44:59.610 --> 00:45:00.090
And yeah.
没错。

917
00:45:00.590 --> 00:45:02.710
So that's that's our little reference to that.
所以那是我们对那集的一个小致敬。

918
00:45:03.110 --> 00:45:03.210
Yeah.
是啊。

919
00:45:03.470 --> 00:45:08.010
But there's the references to like the whole history up to this point, I think, in a lot of these little scenes.
但我认为，在很多这些小场景里，都有对这一路走来的整个历史的致敬。

920
00:45:08.310 --> 00:45:12.050
Randy Cordray sent me the call sheets for this episode.
兰迪·科德雷把这集的通告单发给了我。

921
00:45:12.050 --> 00:45:16.930
And I was able to look at the call sheet for Steve's final shooting day.
我得以看到了史蒂夫最后拍摄那一天的通告单。

922
00:45:17.450 --> 00:45:18.910
That scene in the break room.
休息室里的那场戏。

923
00:45:19.110 --> 00:45:20.310
That was first up.
那是第一场拍的。

924
00:45:20.450 --> 00:45:22.510
We shot that at 7 a.m.
我们早上七点就拍了那场戏。

925
00:45:22.510 --> 00:45:24.170
That was one of the scenes on his last day.
那是他最后一天拍摄的场景之一。

926
00:45:24.310 --> 00:45:27.670
And then this scene where he's freaking out and he calls Holly.
还有他情绪崩溃给霍莉打电话的那场戏。

927
00:45:27.790 --> 00:45:29.190
This was also on his last day.
这也是在他最后一天拍的。

928
00:45:29.390 --> 00:45:35.530
You mentioned that Paul Feig sort of stacked his day with the most sentimental, most emotional moments.
你提到保罗·费格把最感人、最走心的时刻都堆在了他最后一天。

929
00:45:35.850 --> 00:45:36.610
He had to cry all day.
他那天几乎哭了一整天。

930
00:45:36.610 --> 00:45:37.390
Basically, yeah.
基本上是这样。

931
00:45:37.850 --> 00:45:44.490
Well, he was I mean, by the time it got to the Jim Michael scene, that was the biggest difficult one to edit.
嗯，我是说，当拍到吉姆和迈克尔的那场戏时，那是剪辑起来最困难的一场。

932
00:45:44.670 --> 00:45:49.030
I mean, they were both just complete messes in that scene.
我是说，那场戏里他们俩都完全崩溃了。

933
00:45:49.330 --> 00:45:53.010
I mean, I kept running into Paul Feig saying, tell them to dry it up somehow.
我当时不停地跑去跟保罗·费格说，让他们想办法收敛一点。

934
00:45:53.570 --> 00:45:53.770
Yeah.
是啊。

935
00:45:54.070 --> 00:45:54.950
It's too much.
太过了。

936
00:45:55.670 --> 00:46:01.350
Well, when Steve is Michael's voice, you know, it cracks when he goes, you came here as a young man.
当史蒂夫用迈克尔的声音说出“你当年还是个年轻人来到这里”时，他的声音都在颤抖。

937
00:46:01.590 --> 00:46:03.690
I was like crying.
我当时都看哭了。

938
00:46:04.790 --> 00:46:09.950
Coming up is one of my favorite scenes because Michael is going to have to say goodbye to Toby.
接下来是我最喜欢的场景之一，因为迈克尔不得不跟托比道别。

939
00:46:10.330 --> 00:46:14.750
And he has to do his best to not say something awful to Toby.
他必须尽力不对托比说出什么难听的话。

940
00:46:14.890 --> 00:46:15.810
And he does it.
而且他做到了。

941
00:46:16.070 --> 00:46:17.150
It is amazing.
真是太棒了。

942
00:46:17.170 --> 00:46:22.210
Even when Toby tells him that he has a brother in Colorado.
即使当托比告诉他自己在科罗拉多有个兄弟的时候。

943
00:46:22.210 --> 00:46:26.950
I mean, Michael cannot get away from this family of wet blankets.
我是说，迈克尔简直逃不出这群扫兴鬼的魔掌。

944
00:46:26.950 --> 00:46:28.190
The look on Michael's face.
迈克尔脸上的表情。

945
00:46:28.650 --> 00:46:29.710
When he's like, what?
当他那种“什么？”的表情出现时。

946
00:46:30.130 --> 00:46:34.150
And you know, like that gif that of him just going, no, no.
你知道的，就像那个他喊着“不，不”的动图一样。

947
00:46:34.410 --> 00:46:38.030
Like, you know, that's what is going on inside of his head.
你知道，那就是他脑子里正在想的事情。

948
00:46:39.110 --> 00:46:40.310
But he does it.
但他还是做到了。

949
00:46:40.630 --> 00:46:42.750
And then Kelly just wants him to walk away.
然后凯莉只想让他赶紧走开。

950
00:46:43.050 --> 00:46:43.230
Yeah.
是啊。

951
00:46:43.730 --> 00:46:50.850
But then I guess, is this another greatest hits when he gives Ryan his St. Paulie girl neon sign in his quiet closet?
不过我猜，当他在那个安静的壁橱里把圣保利女孩的霓虹灯牌送给瑞安时，这算不算又一次“精选集”时刻？

952
00:46:50.850 --> 00:46:52.990
His whole closet is blue.
他的整个壁橱都是蓝色的。

953
00:46:53.350 --> 00:46:53.670
Yeah.
是啊。

954
00:46:53.970 --> 00:46:54.670
It's funny.
真逗。

955
00:46:54.790 --> 00:46:58.790
The one with, we didn't mention it going by, with Phyllis and her mitten.
还有那个，我们刚才没提，菲利斯和她的连指手套。

956
00:46:59.030 --> 00:46:59.410
Oh, yes.
哦，没错。

957
00:46:59.410 --> 00:47:01.970
But that's a reference to the first Christmas episode.
那是对第一集圣诞特辑的致敬。

958
00:47:02.310 --> 00:47:02.610
Yes.
是的。

959
00:47:02.750 --> 00:47:06.030
And he hated that stupid oven mitt that she made for him.
他当时特别讨厌她给他织的那副蠢手套。

960
00:47:06.230 --> 00:47:09.930
And I love that she's really testing his maturity here.
我特别喜欢她在这里考验他成熟度的方式。

961
00:47:10.070 --> 00:47:15.430
Because the description that she has of this mitten and how you're supposed to clean it, it's like the worst gift.
因为她对这副手套的描述，以及该怎么清洗它，简直是史上最烂的礼物。

962
00:47:15.430 --> 00:47:17.370
It just gets worse and worse.
而且越听越离谱。

963
00:47:17.710 --> 00:47:18.050
She's like, you can't wash it.
她说，你不能洗它。

964
00:47:18.150 --> 00:47:19.390
It has to be air dried.
必须自然风干。

965
00:47:19.590 --> 00:47:20.150
It's like got all these.
还有各种各样的要求。

966
00:47:20.150 --> 00:47:20.950
You can't get it wet.
不能沾水。

967
00:47:20.970 --> 00:47:21.610
You can't wear them outside.
不能戴着它出门。

968
00:47:21.950 --> 00:47:22.590
Like all these things.
诸如此类的规矩。

969
00:47:22.610 --> 00:47:22.810
Yeah.
没错。

970
00:47:22.930 --> 00:47:25.270
It's this horrible, useless mitten.
就是一副糟糕透顶、毫无用处的手套。

971
00:47:25.490 --> 00:47:26.530
And he's so nice to her.
但他对她还挺好的。

972
00:47:26.770 --> 00:47:29.570
But you know exactly what he wants to say.
但你完全能猜到他心里想说什么。

973
00:47:29.770 --> 00:47:29.930
Yeah.
是啊。

974
00:47:31.030 --> 00:47:33.190
So there are a few really great deleted scenes, Greg.
格雷格，有几个删减片段真的很棒。

975
00:47:33.350 --> 00:47:33.990
They're on the DVD.
都在DVD里。

976
00:47:34.430 --> 00:47:36.490
And I wanted to ask you about one of them.
我想问你其中一个片段。

977
00:47:36.770 --> 00:47:43.210
When Michael is having this moment in the break room where he's getting emotional, kind of I'm toggling back here for a second.
当迈克尔在休息室里情绪有些激动的时候，我稍微往回倒一下。

978
00:47:43.890 --> 00:47:50.650
There is this beat that didn't make it to the air episode where he takes off his boots and throws them in the trash.
正片里没剪进去的一段是，他脱下靴子扔进了垃圾桶。

979
00:47:50.890 --> 00:47:51.270
Yeah.
没错。

980
00:47:51.490 --> 00:47:54.670
Those boots that he had on the roof is like, boots, I'm going to Colorado.
就是他在屋顶上穿的那双靴子，他说“靴子，我要去科罗拉多”。

981
00:47:55.070 --> 00:47:57.750
And then ultimately Creed ends up wearing them.
最后克里德捡去穿了。

982
00:47:58.070 --> 00:47:59.310
He finds them in the trash.
他在垃圾桶里翻出来的。

983
00:47:59.930 --> 00:48:00.070
Yeah.
是啊。

984
00:48:00.250 --> 00:48:02.330
But was that from a personal story for you?
那是源于你的亲身经历吗？

985
00:48:02.330 --> 00:48:03.170
Yeah, that was a personal story.
对，那是我的亲身经历。

986
00:48:03.470 --> 00:48:10.770
I kind of think that the boots were a bigger deal in my first draft of the script because I think you barely see them on the rooftop.
我觉得在剧本初稿里，靴子的戏份比这重，因为在屋顶上你几乎看不清它们。

987
00:48:11.050 --> 00:48:11.890
I noticed them.
我注意到了。

988
00:48:12.050 --> 00:48:12.330
Oh, right away.
哦，一眼就看到了。

989
00:48:12.330 --> 00:48:12.950
Very clearly.
非常明显。

990
00:48:13.250 --> 00:48:16.630
I clocked that Michael was wearing cowboy boots.
我一眼就看出迈克尔穿的是牛仔靴。

991
00:48:16.870 --> 00:48:17.890
A student brings.
学生带来的。

992
00:48:17.890 --> 00:48:19.950
I did not deep dive cowboy boots, though.
不过我没深究牛仔靴的事。

993
00:48:20.150 --> 00:48:20.350
Yeah.
是啊。

994
00:48:20.530 --> 00:48:22.290
But that happened to me.
但那事确实发生在我身上。

995
00:48:22.290 --> 00:48:30.870
I went to visit Austin, Texas, and I got very inspired to buy a pair of cowboy boots while I was there because everybody had cowboy boots.
我去德克萨斯州的奥斯汀玩，在那儿受了启发，买了一双牛仔靴，因为每个人都穿牛仔靴。

996
00:48:31.070 --> 00:48:34.310
And I brought them back and was wearing them in New York.
我把它带回纽约，穿在脚上。

997
00:48:34.310 --> 00:48:40.210
And I decided I was walking from my apartment to my job at Saturday Night Live wearing these cowboy boots.
我决定穿着这双牛仔靴从公寓走到《周六夜现场》上班。

998
00:48:40.370 --> 00:48:41.430
How big of a walk was that?
那得走多远啊？

999
00:48:41.530 --> 00:48:46.150
It was like two miles, you know, on the concrete of New York in the cowboy boots.
大概两英里吧，你知道的，穿着牛仔靴走在纽约的水泥地上。

1000
00:48:46.150 --> 00:48:53.290
So by the time I got there, I was like, you know, I've got like flat feet and just really, really should not be wearing cowboy boots.
所以等我走到那儿的时候，我就想，你知道，我是扁平足，真的真的不该穿牛仔靴。

1001
00:48:53.650 --> 00:49:00.670
And anyway, they were so painful that I took them off and threw them out and got a pair of sneakers.
总之，它们太疼了，我就把它们脱掉扔了，换了一双运动鞋。

1002
00:49:01.110 --> 00:49:01.410
And A.
还有A。

1003
00:49:01.530 --> 00:49:11.610
Whitney Brown, who was this writer on Saturday Night Live who had a much more authentic country background, he had his grandmother's recipe for vittles,
惠特尼·布朗，他是《周六夜现场》的一位编剧，有着更地道的乡村背景，他有他祖母传下来的“干粮”食谱，

1004
00:49:11.950 --> 00:49:15.870
which was like a squirrel or something on his wall.
那东西就像是他墙上挂的松鼠之类的玩意儿。

1005
00:49:16.150 --> 00:49:17.890
And maybe not flat feet.
也许不是因为扁平足。

1006
00:49:18.170 --> 00:49:18.910
Yeah, probably not.
是啊，大概不是。

1007
00:49:19.010 --> 00:49:19.810
He fished them out.
他把它们捞了出来。

1008
00:49:19.890 --> 00:49:23.470
And I swear he wore them every day for the rest of the time that I was on that show.
我发誓，在我待在那节目的余下时间里，他每天都穿着那双鞋。

1009
00:49:24.170 --> 00:49:25.430
He was your creed.
他就是你的克里德。

1010
00:49:25.570 --> 00:49:26.690
Yeah, he was the creed.
没错，他就是克里德。

1011
00:49:26.870 --> 00:49:29.750
So anyway, I cribbed that joke, that little bit.
总之，我抄了那个笑话，那个小桥段。

1012
00:49:29.870 --> 00:49:33.330
But it was a deleted scene because it was probably more meaningful to me than anybody else.
但那是个删减片段，因为它对我来说可能比对别人更有意义。

1013
00:49:35.110 --> 00:49:43.290
But I do think it was good because creed, I can't remember what the blow to that scene was, but I feel like creed says something like, you think it really was the boots?
但我确实觉得它不错，因为克里德——我不记得那场戏的结尾是什么了，但我感觉克里德说了类似这样的话：你觉得真的是因为靴子吗？

1014
00:49:43.850 --> 00:49:45.670
And then they're like, no, we don't think it.
然后他们说，不，我们不这么认为。

1015
00:49:45.690 --> 00:49:46.590
We think it was something emotional.
我们觉得是因为某种情感原因。

1016
00:49:46.710 --> 00:49:47.170
He's like, good.
他说，很好。

1017
00:49:47.230 --> 00:49:48.210
And he grabs the boots out.
然后他把靴子拿了出来。

1018
00:49:48.350 --> 00:49:48.510
Yeah.
是啊。

1019
00:49:48.590 --> 00:49:49.290
Like, where's them?
就像是，它们在哪儿？

1020
00:49:49.290 --> 00:49:51.350
You want to make sure it was okay to take the boots.
你想确认拿走靴子没问题。

1021
00:49:51.350 --> 00:49:52.150
Yeah, he's just carried about the boots.
对，他只是很在意那双靴子。

1022
00:49:52.150 --> 00:49:55.610
Oh, is Michael like kind of teary when he throws the boots away?
哦，迈克尔扔掉靴子的时候是不是有点热泪盈眶？

1023
00:49:55.810 --> 00:49:56.070
Yeah.
是啊。

1024
00:49:56.230 --> 00:49:57.590
I mean, he's emotional the whole time.
我是说，他全程都很情绪化。

1025
00:49:57.650 --> 00:49:57.970
Yeah.
没错。

1026
00:49:58.530 --> 00:49:59.710
And he says that his feet hurt or something.
他说他脚疼什么的。

1027
00:49:59.810 --> 00:50:00.650
That's why he throws the boots away.
这就是他扔掉靴子的原因。

1028
00:50:00.650 --> 00:50:00.930
Yeah.
是啊。

1029
00:50:01.050 --> 00:50:02.530
But the boots are also supposed to be-
但靴子也应该是——

1030
00:50:02.530 --> 00:50:04.650
I didn't see the deleted scene, so I didn't know what happens in it.
我没看过那个删减片段，所以我不知道里面发生了什么。

1031
00:50:04.770 --> 00:50:08.530
The boots are supposed to be sort of symbolic of his move to Colorado.
靴子象征着他搬去科罗拉多。

1032
00:50:08.730 --> 00:50:11.130
And at this point, he's questioning if he's going to go to Colorado.
而此时，他正在质疑自己是否真的要搬去科罗拉多。

1033
00:50:11.130 --> 00:50:12.350
So he gets rid of his boots.
所以他扔掉了靴子。

1034
00:50:12.690 --> 00:50:12.810
Okay.
好吧。

1035
00:50:12.990 --> 00:50:13.090
Right.
没错。

1036
00:50:13.490 --> 00:50:15.050
So now we're in the conference room.
现在我们到了会议室。

1037
00:50:15.290 --> 00:50:17.750
The party planning committee is still planning this party.
派对策划委员会还在策划这个派对。

1038
00:50:18.110 --> 00:50:19.250
They're so slow.
她们太慢了。

1039
00:50:20.110 --> 00:50:22.970
Meredith would like to get an erotic cake.
梅雷迪思想要一个色情蛋糕。

1040
00:50:23.390 --> 00:50:23.770
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1041
00:50:24.390 --> 00:50:29.350
And she said they're really great because they have real women depicted on the cakes.
她说那些蛋糕真的很棒，因为上面画着真实的女性形象。

1042
00:50:29.630 --> 00:50:29.770
Yeah.
是啊。

1043
00:50:29.930 --> 00:50:33.390
And Phyllis is like a someone who buys a lot of erotic cakes.
菲利斯就像那种经常买色情蛋糕的人。

1044
00:50:33.590 --> 00:50:35.250
It just feels good to be represented.
能被表现出来感觉真好。

1045
00:50:35.950 --> 00:50:37.050
I love this scene.
我喜欢这一幕。

1046
00:50:37.170 --> 00:50:40.650
I don't think this was in my writer's draft.
我觉得这不在我最初的编剧草稿里。

1047
00:50:40.770 --> 00:50:42.530
I feel like there's a BJ in here.
我觉得这里面有B.J.的手笔。

1048
00:50:42.670 --> 00:50:44.310
I feel like this is a room-written scene.
我觉得这是编剧室集体创作的场景。

1049
00:50:44.510 --> 00:50:45.450
It's very funny, though.
不过这真的很有趣。

1050
00:50:45.650 --> 00:50:46.890
It's interesting you say that.
你这么说很有意思。

1051
00:50:47.030 --> 00:50:48.570
This was an extra scene.
这是一个额外片段。

1052
00:50:48.570 --> 00:50:54.590
I guess when you guys got permission to supersize this episode, we got that news a little late.
我想当你们获准延长这一集时长时，我们收到消息有点晚了。

1053
00:50:54.690 --> 00:50:58.650
And we did shoot a couple of things that did not involve Steve.
我们确实拍了一些不涉及史蒂夫的戏份。

1054
00:50:58.770 --> 00:50:59.770
They couldn't because he was gone.
他们没法拍，因为他已经离开了。

1055
00:50:59.930 --> 00:51:01.450
We shot this a week later.
我们是一周后拍的这段。

1056
00:51:01.630 --> 00:51:02.990
This was one of them.
这是其中之一。

1057
00:51:03.170 --> 00:51:04.950
I do have a continuity catch.
我发现了一个连贯性问题。

1058
00:51:05.230 --> 00:51:09.910
At 14 minutes, 51 seconds, did anyone notice that Angela Martin now has her hair down?
在14分51秒的时候，有人注意到安吉拉·马丁的头发散下来了吗？

1059
00:51:10.250 --> 00:51:10.750
No.
没有。

1060
00:51:10.750 --> 00:51:18.630
The whole entire episode, she has her hair pulled back in a clip, and then all of a sudden, in this extra party planning committee scene, her hair is down.
整整一集，她的头发都是用发夹盘起来的，结果突然在这个额外的派对策划委员会场景里，她的头发就散下来了。

1061
00:51:18.810 --> 00:51:21.090
I noticed that my hair is much prettier.
我注意到我的头发好看多了。

1062
00:51:21.850 --> 00:51:27.550
Somehow, the way we did my hair, it turned out prettier than the original week of shooting.
不知怎么的，我那天的发型比最初拍摄那一周还要好看。

1063
00:51:27.750 --> 00:51:33.850
So, clearly, there were some continuity photo issues because someone did not notice that your hair had been up.
所以很明显，当时出现了一些连贯性照片的问题，因为有人没注意到你的头发本来是盘起来的。

1064
00:51:33.970 --> 00:51:35.530
And why didn't I notice?
为什么我没注意到呢？

1065
00:51:35.530 --> 00:51:39.190
I had just filmed this episode when they didn't put the clip in.
我拍这一集的时候，他们没给我戴发夹。

1066
00:51:39.270 --> 00:51:40.770
I didn't even register it.
我甚至都没意识到这一点。

1067
00:51:40.890 --> 00:51:42.150
Do you remember that kind of stuff?
你记得那种细节吗？

1068
00:51:42.310 --> 00:51:43.770
You got to, I guess, as an actor.
我想作为演员，你得记得。

1069
00:51:43.910 --> 00:51:44.090
Sometimes, yeah.
有时候会吧。

1070
00:51:44.270 --> 00:51:46.410
I mean, there are many times where I'd be like, oh, no, no, no.
我是说，有很多次我会觉得，噢，不不不。

1071
00:51:46.410 --> 00:51:47.790
I had my hair in a braid for that.
我拍那场戏时头发是编起来的。

1072
00:51:47.990 --> 00:51:50.850
But for whatever reason, I didn't catch it on this day.
但不知为何，那天我没发现这个问题。

1073
00:51:50.930 --> 00:51:54.090
Well, maybe the topic of erotic cakes made you relax.
嗯，也许是关于色情蛋糕的话题让你放松警惕了。

1074
00:51:54.210 --> 00:51:55.110
Take your hair clip out.
把发夹取下来。

1075
00:51:55.610 --> 00:51:56.470
Shake your hair out.
把头发甩开。

1076
00:51:56.470 --> 00:51:57.090
Yeah, exactly.
没错，就是这样。

1077
00:51:57.930 --> 00:52:00.810
Well, Michael is going to approach Pam, but she's rushing out.
迈克尔本来要去找帕姆，但她正匆忙离开。

1078
00:52:01.130 --> 00:52:02.930
Yeah, that was shot on the last day.
对，那场戏是最后一天拍的。

1079
00:52:02.930 --> 00:52:06.190
That scene of me in the bullpen with Steve.
就是我和史蒂夫在办公区的那场戏。

1080
00:52:06.430 --> 00:52:13.230
The other storyline that's going on that we haven't talked about is that Gabe is really just kind of aggressively trying to get Erin back.
我们还没聊到的另一条故事线是，盖博正非常激进地想要追回艾琳。

1081
00:52:13.490 --> 00:52:16.690
And he keeps going in the restroom to look for her.
他不停地跑进洗手间去找她。

1082
00:52:16.930 --> 00:52:18.570
He's kind of getting aggressive with Andy.
他对安迪也变得有点咄咄逼人。

1083
00:52:18.810 --> 00:52:26.270
But at 16 minutes, 15 seconds, we have a great callback to women's appreciation because Creed is going to come out of the women's restroom.
但在16分15秒，我们有一个对“女性欣赏日”的精彩呼应，因为克里德要从女洗手间走出来。

1084
00:52:27.310 --> 00:52:29.030
That's where he does his number twos.
那是他解决大号的地方。

1085
00:52:29.190 --> 00:52:30.210
He's made that clear.
他已经说得很清楚了。

1086
00:52:30.370 --> 00:52:31.290
It's much nicer in there.
那里面舒服多了。

1087
00:52:31.290 --> 00:52:35.230
I don't know if we've been in the restroom since women's appreciation.
我不知道自“女性欣赏日”之后我们有没有再进过那个洗手间。

1088
00:52:35.570 --> 00:52:36.310
The women's?
女洗手间吗？

1089
00:52:36.430 --> 00:52:37.410
I don't know if we have.
我不知道有没有。

1090
00:52:37.630 --> 00:52:38.350
I mean, the men's?
我是说，男洗手间呢？

1091
00:52:38.350 --> 00:52:43.270
We've been in the men's quite a bit with Michael, but I think you're right.
我们倒是经常跟着迈克尔去男洗手间，但我觉得你说得对。

1092
00:52:43.270 --> 00:52:45.910
I'm not sure we've been back into the women's restroom.
我不确定我们是否回过女洗手间。

1093
00:52:46.090 --> 00:52:49.010
I love the gym line at the beginning of this.
我很喜欢开头那句关于健身房的台词。

1094
00:52:49.170 --> 00:52:50.690
It's like, so you're filming in the restroom?
就像是，所以你们是在洗手间里拍摄吗？

1095
00:52:50.850 --> 00:52:52.270
You're filming us going to the bathroom now?
你们现在连我们上厕所都要拍吗？

1096
00:52:52.470 --> 00:52:52.650
Yeah.
是啊。

1097
00:52:53.030 --> 00:52:54.190
That was really well done.
那段拍得真好。

1098
00:52:55.250 --> 00:52:59.390
Zach Woods is hilarious in this thing where he's just threatening Andy.
扎克·伍兹在威胁安迪的那段戏里简直太搞笑了。

1099
00:52:59.390 --> 00:53:03.970
He's the type of actor for me that anything he says is just hilarious to me.
对我来说，他是那种无论说什么都让我觉得好笑的演员。

1100
00:53:04.170 --> 00:53:06.850
Like, I would always laugh if I was in a scene with him.
如果我和他演对手戏，我肯定会一直笑场。

1101
00:53:07.230 --> 00:53:11.110
Well, coming up, we're going to meet Toby's brother, Rory, on a video call.
接下来，我们将通过视频通话见见托比的兄弟罗里。

1102
00:53:11.610 --> 00:53:16.570
Toby is going to let Rory know about Michael coming to Colorado.
托比打算告诉罗里迈克尔要来科罗拉多州的事。

1103
00:53:17.250 --> 00:53:21.990
Rory would like to know if Michael likes jam, because he could give him a basket of jam.
罗里想知道迈克尔喜不喜欢果酱，因为他可以送他一篮子果酱。

1104
00:53:22.170 --> 00:53:23.210
He has lots of jaMs.
他有很多果酱。

1105
00:53:23.730 --> 00:53:25.810
We had a fan question from Hannah L.
我们收到一个来自加利福尼亚州汉娜·L的粉丝提问。

1106
00:53:26.090 --> 00:53:27.110
in California.
在加利福尼亚州。

1107
00:53:27.470 --> 00:53:32.370
Is Toby's Colorado brother, played by Paul Lieberstein's real brother, Warren?
托比在科罗拉多州的兄弟是由保罗·利伯斯坦现实中的兄弟沃伦饰演的吗？

1108
00:53:32.910 --> 00:53:34.770
If so, how did this come about?
如果是的话，这是怎么促成的？

1109
00:53:34.930 --> 00:53:36.150
Was it planned for a while?
这是计划已久的吗？

1110
00:53:36.370 --> 00:53:37.950
Was this a card on the writer's wall?
这是编剧墙上的一个点子吗？

1111
00:53:37.950 --> 00:53:44.510
So, now, I remember Warren and Paul talking about this, and I remember them kicking around
现在，我记得沃伦和保罗讨论过这件事，我记得他们当时在琢磨

